„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚsaying, I am Alpha and Omega, the first and the last: and, What thou seest, write in a book, and send it unto the seven churches which are in Asia; unto Ephesus, and unto Smyrna, and unto Pergamos, and unto Thyatira, and unto Sardis, and unto Philadelphia, and unto Laodicea.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤bookA§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdAnd I turned to see the voice that spake with me. And being turned, I saw seven golden candlesticks;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸand in the midst of the seven candlesticks one like unto the Son of man, clothed with a garment down to the foot, and girt about the paps with a golden girdle.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdHis head and his hairs were white like wool, as white as snow; and his eyes were as a flame of fire;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmand his feet like unto fine brass, as if they burned in a furnace; and his voice as the sound of many waters.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—And he had in his right hand seven stars: and out of his mouth went a sharp twoedged sword: and his countenance was as the sun shineth in his strength.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤bookA§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAnd when I saw him, I fell at his feet as dead. And he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not; I am the first and the last:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvI am he that liveth, and was dead; and, behold, I am alive for evermore, Amen; and have the keys of hell and of death.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiWrite the things which thou hast seen, and the things which are, and the things which shall be hereafter;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙàthe mystery of the seven stars which thou sawest in my right hand,